From: Package maintainers <packages@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] fix settings.ini layered load order
Source: downstream
Upstream: not submitted; suitable for upstream review

gtk_settings_init() loads every settings.ini it finds with the same
GTK_SETTINGS_SOURCE_DEFAULT source, so the last file read overwrites every
property an earlier file set and load order alone decides priority.

Two ordering mistakes follow from that. First, the compiled sysconfdir file
(_gtk_get_sysconfdir(), "/etc" on this build since Meson defaults sysconfdir
to "/etc" whenever prefix is "/usr") is loaded before the
g_get_system_config_dirs() walk, so any directory in that walk overrides the
administrator's compiled-sysconfdir file. Second, the walk itself reads
XDG_CONFIG_DIRS forward from index zero, but XDG_CONFIG_DIRS lists its
highest-priority directory first. The shipped desktop exports
XDG_CONFIG_DIRS=/etc/xdg:/run/xdg:/usr/share/xdg, so the forward walk lets
/usr/share/xdg/gtk-4.0/settings.ini (vendor) load last and override
/run/xdg/gtk-4.0/settings.ini (runtime) and /etc/xdg/gtk-4.0/settings.ini
(administrator), inverting Nex's vendor below runtime below administrator
priority.

Walk XDG_CONFIG_DIRS backwards so its highest-priority directory loads last,
and load the compiled sysconfdir file after that walk so the administrator's
compiled-sysconfdir file still beats every XDG_CONFIG_DIRS entry, including
the administrator's own /etc/xdg entry. This mirrors the direct GTK3
precedent in gtk3-uapi-multipress.patch. The vendor-prefix read
(_gtk_get_data_prefix()/share) and the user-config read
(g_get_user_config_dir()) already load first and last respectively and keep
their existing positions.

diff -urN a/gtk/gtksettings.c b/gtk/gtksettings.c
--- a/gtk/gtksettings.c
+++ b/gtk/gtksettings.c
@@ -282,18 +282,28 @@
   gtk_settings_load_from_key_file (settings, path, GTK_SETTINGS_SOURCE_DEFAULT);
   g_free (path);

-  path = g_build_filename (_gtk_get_sysconfdir (), "gtk-4.0", "settings.ini", NULL);
-  gtk_settings_load_from_key_file (settings, path, GTK_SETTINGS_SOURCE_DEFAULT);
-  g_free (path);
-
+  /*
+   * Every file here is loaded with the same source, so a later file overwrites
+   * an earlier one and load order alone decides priority. XDG_CONFIG_DIRS
+   * lists its highest-priority directory first, so walk it backwards, and load
+   * the compiled sysconfdir file afterwards so the administrator's
+   * compiled-sysconfdir file stays above both the vendor prefix and the
+   * directory list, including that list's own administrator entry.
+   */
   config_dirs = g_get_system_config_dirs ();
   for (i = 0; config_dirs[i] != NULL; i++)
+    ;
+  while (i-- > 0)
     {
       path = g_build_filename (config_dirs[i], "gtk-4.0", "settings.ini", NULL);
       gtk_settings_load_from_key_file (settings, path, GTK_SETTINGS_SOURCE_DEFAULT);
       g_free (path);
     }

+  path = g_build_filename (_gtk_get_sysconfdir (), "gtk-4.0", "settings.ini", NULL);
+  gtk_settings_load_from_key_file (settings, path, GTK_SETTINGS_SOURCE_DEFAULT);
+  g_free (path);
+
   path = g_build_filename (g_get_user_config_dir (), "gtk-4.0", "settings.ini", NULL);
   gtk_settings_load_from_key_file (settings, path, GTK_SETTINGS_SOURCE_DEFAULT);
   g_free (path);
